KosmicKrisp: fillModeNonSolid and geometryStreams (DXVK requires both).
- Polygons drawn as points: Metal has no point fill mode, so the geometry stage (emulated, the
  same passthrough geometry shader transform feedback uses when there is none) emits each
  vertex as a 1.0-sized point. Face culling is not applied to them, and with transform feedback
  the pipeline keeps filling.
- Geometry shaders with several vertex streams: the shared lowering already handles them; only
  stream 0 is rasterized (no rasterization stream select), and transform feedback queries are
  kept per stream.

